/wudict
# The Windows desktop binary (build-windows.cmd): the same product `make build`
# writes, with the extension Windows needs to exec it.
/wudict.exe
dist/**
docs.local/
*_NOTRACK.md
coverage.out
/wudict.toml
/state.json
.DS_Store

# Local Android Studio / IntelliJ settings.
.idea/

# Android (D52) — build outputs and the cross-compiled server lib.
# gradle-wrapper.jar is NOT ignored: it is the build, committed.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/build-sh/
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
# The x86_64 server for the emulator (build-android.cmd `intel`). It sits in a
# source dir no variant reads unless build.gradle is told to, so it can never
# reach an APK by accident - but it is still a 16 MB build product, not source.
android/app/src/emuX86/jniLibs/
android/local.properties
/build-android.local.bat
/CLAUDE.local.md
code-review/
# Local corpus for manual checks (real dictionaries: too big to ship, and not
# ours to license). Point DICT_DIR at it for a representative preview.
/test_data/

# Play release (fastlane). The lanes and the listing ARE tracked -
# fastlane/metadata/android/ is also the layout F-Droid reads. What must never
# be committed is the local tooling and every piece of signing material.
/Makefile_fastlane
/fastlane.md
/play-store-config.json
*.jks
*.keystore
/upload_certificate.pem
/playconsole/
/fastlane/report.xml
/fastlane/README.md
/vendor/bundle/
# Fuzz regression seeds under testdata/fuzz are source, not scratch outputs.

# The local dictionary-comparison oracle (a Qt/CMake build kept outside the
# project's own tooling): the build tree and the results it writes are products
# of a hand-run tool, never source. Ignoring these leaves the directory itself
# listable, so a future source file in it would still show up.
/tools/dslcompare/build/
/tools/dslcompare/results/
# Bytecode of the Python tools in tools/ (csvorjson2wudict.py and friends).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent tooling: plans and scratch written by coding sessions, never part of
# the product (HANDOFF.md leaves it alone for the same reason).
/.zcode/
